• Over 14,000 households adopting FLA practices with 35,000 people benefitting from increased dietary diversity (DISCOVER Project Malawi);
• Training and capacity building of 2300 government extension staff and FLA applied among 100,000 families in Malawi benefitting from improved livelihood security and resilience to climate change resilience (‘BETTER’ Project Malawi);
• 3,000 farmers benefitting from the ‘PRESERVE Kafue’ project in Zambia, with indirect benefits for 15,000 relating to improved food security, enhanced nutrition and resilience.

